1
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,440
Hi there! This is LayerCue.

2
00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:11,830
It puts your show on the big screen, in layers.

3
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,910
It runs on Mac and Windows.

4
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:16,620
Here, a video runs underneath.

5
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:18,240
Words sit on top.

6
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:20,570
And a logo stays up in the corner.

7
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:23,010
Each one comes and goes on its own.

8
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:27,040
In this episode, we'll walk around the main window.

9
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:28,630
Today we just look.

10
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,640
You won't send anything out yet.

11
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:34,550
The window has four areas.

12
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:36,280
The sidebar on the left.

13
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:37,990
Your slides in the middle.

14
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:40,160
The stage band across the top.

15
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:42,420
And the status bar along the bottom.

16
00:00:42,990 --> 00:00:45,240
Here's an easy way to remember it.

17
00:00:45,310 --> 00:00:46,650
Pick on the left.

18
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,010
Click in the middle.

19
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:49,390
Watch the top.

20
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:50,920
Adjust on the right.

21
00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:54,970
Adjust means Slide settings, at the far right of the band.

22
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:58,570
Let's start on the left.

23
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,350
Cue Sheets are at the top.

24
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:03,470
A cue sheet is the running order for one event.

25
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:06,510
This one, Tour, lines up six short guides.

26
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:09,500
Below the line is the Library drawer.

27
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:12,480
A library is a folder of presentations.

28
00:01:12,550 --> 00:01:15,420
And a presentation is one set of slides.

29
00:01:15,490 --> 00:01:18,530
The number on the right is how many slides it has.

30
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,500
Press the double arrow to pull the drawer up.

31
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:23,880
Press it again to lower it.

32
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:25,960
Just pointing at it won't raise it.

33
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:31,080
Now I'll click Start here, inside the Tour cue sheet.

34
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:34,420
The middle shows every presentation in it, in order.

35
00:01:34,790 --> 00:01:38,300
Each one has a title bar with its name and slide count.

36
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:40,340
On the right are five buttons.

37
00:01:40,410 --> 00:01:41,590
Add File.

38
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:42,640
Link.

39
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:43,670
Edit.

40
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:45,280
Layer for this list.

41
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:47,290
And Presentation settings.

42
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:49,900
Below the bar are the slide cards.

43
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:53,190
Under each picture, you'll see its kind and its name.

44
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:56,840
Here's the big one: a click on the picture sends it out.

45
00:01:56,910 --> 00:01:59,560
No confirmation, no second step.

46
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:02,240
So we won't click any pictures today.

47
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:03,980
That's Episode 3.

48
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:08,010
Up top is where you watch the stage.

49
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:10,240
The tile on the left is Screen 1.

50
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:13,770
Here it's a virtual screen, so no projector is needed.

51
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:17,200
The switch at the right end turns the output on and off.

52
00:02:17,570 --> 00:02:21,460
Under the preview, Layers shown picks what this monitor shows.

53
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:25,240
Beside the preview, the layer column shows what's up right now.

54
00:02:25,310 --> 00:02:27,800
Clear at the top, then seven layers.

55
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:29,240
Five overlays.

56
00:02:29,310 --> 00:02:30,770
F for foreground.

57
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:32,430
And B for background.

58
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,740
Next comes the sound meter.

59
00:02:34,810 --> 00:02:37,380
Then Music, which has its own channel.

60
00:02:37,450 --> 00:02:39,870
And at the right end, Slide settings.

61
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:43,590
Option-click a slide to look at it here, without sending it.

62
00:02:45,510 --> 00:02:48,100
The status bar reads from left to right.

63
00:02:48,170 --> 00:02:49,450
Show and Edit.

64
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:52,630
The On air chip counts the monitors that are showing.

65
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:55,100
The speaker box is your sound device.

66
00:02:55,170 --> 00:02:57,700
The dot and title tell you what's on stage.

67
00:02:58,070 --> 00:03:00,230
Tell us what's wrong sends us a note.

68
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:02,570
The slider changes the card size.

69
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,660
The pencil is Lock editing.

70
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:06,600
And the gear opens Settings.

71
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,470
Now let's see layers in action.

72
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:13,770
This demo is scripted, and the event is made up.

73
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:16,310
A video goes to the background.

74
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,130
The B cell turns amber.

75
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:20,820
Words go on top, in the foreground.

76
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:22,380
F turns indigo.

77
00:03:22,450 --> 00:03:24,490
A logo goes to overlay one.

78
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,400
And cell 1 turns green.

79
00:03:26,870 --> 00:03:28,530
Now I'll change the words.

80
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,280
The video keeps playing.

81
00:03:30,650 --> 00:03:33,890
The little x next to F takes just the words down.

82
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:36,610
That's the whole idea of layers!

83
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:41,630
One last stop: Edit, in the status bar.

84
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:44,780
The whole window becomes the slide editor.

85
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:47,490
Your slides line up in a strip down the left.

86
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:49,480
Click Show to come back.

87
00:03:49,950 --> 00:03:51,740
And that's the main window!

88
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:56,490
You can now find your way around the whole window.

89
00:03:56,560 --> 00:04:00,460
Next up: Episode 2, Install, First Launch and Settings.

90
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:01,720
See you there!

